  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider an arithmetic series and a geometric series having four initial terms from the set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the last terms of these series are the maximum possible four digit numbers, then the number of common terms in these two series is equal to _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given set<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Given an arithmetic series and a geometric series having the first four terms from the given set.&nbsp;</p><p>Then,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>Geometric&#160;series</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>128</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>256</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>512</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1024</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2048</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4096</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8192</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>Arithmetic&#160;series</mtext><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>256</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>4096</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>For common terms,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>So, common terms are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>256</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4096</mn></math> only.</p>",
